    ("RIV-SPAT-0004", "Machine versus experiential acceptance boundary", "Synthetic/backend evidence is treated as sufficient for rendered Quest/3D, frame-rate, comfort, or end-to-end human acceptance.", ["synthetic-overclaim", "render-not-measured", "device-absent", "latency-confused", "experiential-gate"], ["Identify the executable application, runtime/device, input modality, render timing, user-visible latency, and reconnect/degraded evidence."], "Reopen the waypoint, preserve the historical transition, classify backend measurements as MACHINE_ACCEPTANCE, and require real STEWARD_EXPERIENTIAL_ACCEPTANCE.", "Re-run the factual audit and verify that promotion is withheld until rendered/device evidence exists.", "docs/operations/troubleshooting/checkpoints/RIV-SPAT-0004_MACHINE_VS_EXPERIENTIAL_ACCEPTANCE.md"),
    ("RIV-UI-0013", "Component versus human operator experience boundary", "API/component acceptance is mistaken for a browser-rendered text/artifact or microphone operator experience.", ["api-only", "ui-missing", "fixture-transcription", "attachment-ui-missing", "human-acceptance-missing"], ["Open the bounded `/` surface and inspect visible composer, artifact picker, status, response, and correlation behavior; do not accept direct API tests as experiential evidence."], "Add only the bounded operator surface required by the canonical acceptance; retain fixture/API evidence as lower-level evidence and keep the parent pending until the human interaction occurs.", "Run browser-surface acceptance and then obtain the exact Steward interaction result.", "docs/operations/roadmap/evidence/RV-010_BROWSER_OPERATOR_SURFACE.md"),
