    ("RIV-UI-0015", "Local microphone transcription boundary", "A human-triggered bounded microphone capture is unavailable, produces no text, or its audio retention/correlation boundary is unclear.", ["capture-unavailable", "no-transcription", "duration-overflow", "audio-retention"], ["Inspect only bounded provider identity, duration, transcript presence, and retention metadata; never persist raw audio by default."], "Use the local System.Speech path when available, otherwise return a visible unavailable state; do not open an ambient microphone or add a cloud transcription route.", "Run a user-triggered capture, review transcript in the composer, and verify discard-after-transcription metadata.", "docs/operations/troubleshooting/checkpoints/RIV-UI-0010_TRANSCRIPTION.md"),
    ("RIV-UI-0016", "Artifact reference versus content-understanding boundary", "A reference-only artifact attachment or synthetic/component result is mistaken for provider inspection of the artifact content or human multimodal acceptance.", ["reference-only", "image-understanding-unproven", "api-acceptance", "experiential-acceptance"], ["Inspect provider input and the visible result; confirm whether bytes/content were supplied, and retain reference/provenance evidence separately from content understanding."], "Label the attachment as reference-only when the provider cannot inspect it, reject artifact-only requests with an actionable instruction, and do not promote the parent from API/component evidence alone.", "Run text-plus-reference and artifact-only browser checks, then separately run the approved human non-keyboard interaction; record image understanding only if the provider demonstrably receives and uses image content.", "docs/operations/troubleshooting/checkpoints/RIV-UI-0016_ARTIFACT_CONTENT_ACCEPTANCE.md"),
